# Root attributes — CLOSEOUT-01.
# Scope: release-archive membership only. No text/eol/diff attributes are set
# here, so the existing modules/sow/.gitattributes and
# modules/distillery/.gitattributes keep full control of normalisation for
# their subtrees. Git resolves attributes per attribute, not per file, and a
# deeper .gitattributes wins only for attributes it actually sets; neither of
# those files sets export-ignore, so these rules apply unopposed.
#
# export-ignore removes a path from `git archive` ONLY. Every path below stays
# tracked, stays in `git ls-files`, and stays in history.

# X-2 (A-2 / OD-25) — the Phase-1 throwaway spike is not product code. Its
# package-lock pins electron 31.7.7 and extract-zip 2.0.1, the two
# high-severity findings. No product file imports it; the three product
# references to it are prose comments saying it is NOT the real component.
# Excluding it closes C2-RISK-SPIKE-ELECTRON-LOCK-HELD-NONPRODUCT mechanically
# instead of shipping a vulnerable dependency declaration.
# Both forms are required. The `/**` form excludes the CONTENTS; the bare
# directory form excludes the directory ENTRY itself. With only `/**`, git
# archive still emits two empty directory members - measured, not assumed.
modules/sow/tools/spike_compositor export-ignore
modules/sow/tools/spike_compositor/** export-ignore
evidence/cpm1/before-b/modules/sow/tools/spike_compositor export-ignore
evidence/cpm1/before-b/modules/sow/tools/spike_compositor/** export-ignore

# X-3 (A-3 / OD-26) — backup snapshots stay tracked as history but do not ship.
# A distribution carrying two contradicting SBOMs and two contradicting release
# manifests gives a consumer or scanner no rule for which is authoritative.
# Preserving prior records is right; shipping them is not.
#
# Nothing reads these at runtime or during install, verified before excluding:
#   rebase_adapters.py:151-153 tests `backup.exists()` and then WRITES a copy;
#     it never reads a backup's contents. Absent backups are simply recreated.
#   verify_install.ps1 builds its expected path set from the install-time
#     install-manifest.json, not from any committed list, so build and verify
#     stay consistent with each other.
*.pre-CONVERGE01 export-ignore
*.pre-rebase export-ignore

# The directive names the pattern `*.pre-add08`. That pattern matches NOTHING:
# the sole file is evidence/cpm1/baseline/host-hardware.pre-add08.json, where
# `.pre-add08` is an INFIX, not the terminal suffix. Both forms are listed —
# the exact one that matches today, and the suffix form for any future file
# that does end in `.pre-add08`.
*.pre-add08 export-ignore
*.pre-add08.json export-ignore

# X-4 (OD-35) — THE DEVELOPMENT RECORD DOES NOT SHIP. Operator decision,
# 2026-08-30, taken on the STATE-OF-SYSTEM/PUNCH-LIST V6 measurements of
# ENTRY 020. The root evidence/ and dev/ trees are 1931 tracked files at the
# seal and roughly 76% of the archive's bytes. Cutting them from the
# distribution:
#   - removes evidence/cpm1/before-b/modules/sow/config/live_operation.json,
#     the POPULATED authorization switch of N-40. That file's own _comment
#     asserts "This file is gitignored (never committed): a fresh clone stays
#     DENIED-by-absence" — an assertion this repository falsifies, because the
#     file was committed as a checkpoint snapshot. Removing it from the archive
#     makes the assertion true again for a recipient.
#   - removes the developer username and the personal directory tree from the
#     103 and 255 files respectively that carry them.
# History stays tracked; only `git archive` output changes. Nothing in the
# product reads either tree — verified before excluding, over all 1154 tracked
# code files outside them: every runtime path reference is to
# `docs/evidence/...` under modules/sow, which is a DIFFERENT tree and is not
# matched here.
#
# ANCHORING IS LOAD-BEARING. A gitattributes pattern containing no slash is
# matched at every directory depth, so a bare `evidence` would also take
# docs/evidence/ (1 file) and modules/sow/docs/evidence/ (250 files) — the
# receipt tree that ~40 product source files cite by path. The leading slash
# anchors each rule to this file's directory, the repository root. As with X-2,
# both forms are required: the `/**` form excludes the CONTENTS, the bare
# directory form excludes the directory ENTRY itself.
#
# X-2's two evidence/cpm1/before-b/... rules above are now redundant — this
# rule subsumes them. They are left in place rather than deleted so that the
# X-2 record stays legible on its own terms.
/evidence export-ignore
/evidence/** export-ignore
/dev export-ignore
/dev/** export-ignore
